# Verible lint configuration for fpga-low-latency-market-pipeline.
#
# Found automatically by `verible-verilog-ls --rules_config_search` (wired up in
# .claude/plugins/verible-lsp/.lsp.json) and by `verible-verilog-lint
# --rules_config_search`, so editor diagnostics and any CLI lint run agree.
#
# The authoritative lint step stays `verilator --lint-only -Wall` (`make lint`).
# Verible parses each file standalone and never elaborates the design, so it
# cannot see width, driver or connectivity problems and does not replace that
# step. What follows is scoped to defects Verilator does not report.
#
# Deltas only: every rule not named here keeps its Verible default, and the
# defaults stay active alongside these entries. Verified against
# verible-verilog-ls v0.0-4171-ga5e38787 and Verilator 5.032 on 2026-09-09.

# Verilator warns DECLFILENAME when a file name does not match the module it
# declares, which Verible's default-on module-filename already mirrors. This
# extends the same idea to the one-module-per-file layout CLAUDE.md specifies
# for rtl/, which neither of those two rules enforces.
+one-module-per-file

# Verilator errors ENDLABEL on a mismatched module/endmodule label but says
# nothing about begin/end block labels; this covers the block labels.
+mismatched-labels

# Verilator 5.032 -Wall accepts a negative unpacked dimension such as [-2:0]
# without comment. Non-zero-based dimensions have no place in the fixed-point
# core path, so reject them here.
+forbid-negative-array-dim
